@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+## Context
+
+`TaskList.add` already validates title, priority and tags and rejects duplicates, returning a `Result` and leaving the list unchanged on failure. Domain code must not throw, read the clock or use randomness.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+- Goals: a thin parser over `list.add`, reusing its validation and error messages.
+- Non-Goals: quoting or escaping `;`, other formats (CSV), undoing a partial import.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Put `importTasks` in `src/domain/import.ts` and re-export from `src/index.ts`. It only splits lines and calls `list.add`, so validation rules live in one place.
+- Split text on `\r?\n`, each line on `;`. More than three fields is rejected rather than folding extras into tags, since a stray `;` likely means a damaged row.
+- Fewer than three fields is accepted (missing priority/tags), as an assumption for spreadsheet exports that trim trailing empties.
+- Priority is trimmed and matched exactly (case-sensitive), as `add` does; empty becomes `normal`. Tags split on whitespace runs.
+- The reason is the `add` error message; the parser's own errors use the same style.
+- The import is not atomic: valid lines are kept even when others are rejected, as the request asks.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [Titles containing `;` are rejected as too many fields] → documented limitation.
+- [Case-sensitive priorities like `High` are rejected] → the reason names the allowed values.
